                <pb facs="0477" n="379" sameAs="frus:frus1920v01/pg379"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">824.00/89: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Bolivia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Maginnis</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-08-04T17:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 4,
                                1920—5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>52. Department appreciates information contained your numbers 95, July 31, 1
                    p.m., and 96, August 1, 6 p.m., and also the zeal and activity which they
                    reflect, but deems it important to caution you against any statements, which may
                    tend to commit this Government or impair its freedom to act on its own estimate
                    and judgment of situation. Therefore Department desires you to observe
                    instructions contained in Department’s July 21 [<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >20</hi>], 5 p.m., and to confine your representations to junta to questions
                    enumerated in that telegram. …</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Colby</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
